WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.069 --> 00:00:07.850
Edward's first day as a pauper had not gone as he expected.

2
00:00:07.851 --> 00:00:12.231
How did Tom spend that same day?

3
00:00:12.232 --> 00:00:20.431
Left alone in Edward's room, Tom admired himself in the mirror and played with the prince's sword.

4
00:00:20.432 --> 00:00:26.230
"I wish Julian could see me dressed up like this," Tom thought, grinning.

5
00:00:26.231 --> 00:00:31.711
"I look like a real prince!"

6
00:00:31.712 --> 00:00:37.899
He sat on all the chairs and bounced on the bed.

7
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:43.674
He knocked on the suit of armor but didn't dare to try it on.

8
00:00:43.675 --> 00:00:48.378
After half an hour, he was bored and lonely.

9
00:00:48.379 --> 00:00:51.518
He was also beginning to worry.

10
00:00:51.519 --> 00:00:55.089
"Where's Prince Edward?" he thought.

11
00:00:55.090 --> 00:01:00.731
"If anyone catches me wearing his clothes, I'll be locked up in prison forever.

12
00:01:00.732 --> 00:01:05.017
I need to get out of here."

13
00:01:05.018 --> 00:01:09.869
Tom quietly opened the door, and a servant sprang to his feet.

14
00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:12.472
"Your Highness, may I help—"

15
00:01:12.473 --> 00:01:15.571
Tom slammed the door shut.

16
00:01:15.572 --> 00:01:20.541
"That servant thinks I'm Prince Edward!"

17
00:01:20.542 --> 00:01:25.172
Before he could decide what to do next, there was a knock at the door.

18
00:01:25.173 --> 00:01:31.556
The same servant entered and announced, "Lady Jane."

19
00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:35.668
A girl in a beautiful dress ran toward Tom.

20
00:01:35.669 --> 00:01:39.423
But she stopped short when Tom fell to his knees.

21
00:01:39.424 --> 00:01:42.946
"What's wrong, Your Highness?" she said.

22
00:01:42.947 --> 00:01:46.781
"Have mercy on me!" Tom cried.

23
00:01:46.782 --> 00:01:51.785
"I'm not the prince, but only Tom Canty from Offal Street.

24
00:01:51.786 --> 00:01:55.448
Please help me find the prince and return these clothes to him.

25
00:01:55.449 --> 00:02:00.117
Then I'll be on my way and won't trouble any of you again."

26
00:02:00.118 --> 00:02:03.294
"You shouldn't be on your knees, my cousin."

27
00:02:03.295 --> 00:02:06.185
Lady Jane was horrified.

28
00:02:06.186 --> 00:02:10.897
"I should be bowing to you."

29
00:02:10.898 --> 00:02:16.429
She fled the room, which only increased Tom's panic.

30
00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:22.931
"What should I do? What should I do?" he repeated, pacing the floor.

31
00:02:22.932 --> 00:02:27.431
Meanwhile the servant told another servant what he had seen.

32
00:02:27.432 --> 00:02:37.270
"Prince Edward is behaving very strangely and doesn't think he's a prince!"

33
00:02:37.271 --> 00:02:43.498
The news spread rapidly throughout the palace until it reached King Henry.

34
00:02:43.499 --> 00:02:47.798
"The poor boy must be ill," he said.

35
00:02:47.799 --> 00:02:54.420
King Henry immediately issued an order that all talk about Prince Edward's illness must stop.

36
00:02:54.421 --> 00:02:58.439
Anyone who disobeyed would be put to death.

37
00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:04.541
Then he asked for Prince Edward to be brought to him.

38
00:03:04.542 --> 00:03:12.014
Tom didn't understand where Lord Hertford, the prince's chief adviser, was leading him.

39
00:03:12.015 --> 00:03:16.639
They walked down one long corridor after another.

40
00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:22.590
Finally, they entered a grand room, where an old man was lying on a couch.

41
00:03:22.591 --> 00:03:27.111
He sat up and beckoned for Tom to approach.

42
00:03:27.112 --> 00:03:31.339
"My dear son, are you ill?" he said.

43
00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:36.653
"Or are you playing a joke on your father, the king?"

44
00:03:36.654 --> 00:03:39.701
Tom instantly dropped to his knees.

45
00:03:39.702 --> 00:03:45.873
"You're King Henry? Then I'm in real trouble."

46
00:03:45.874 --> 00:03:52.214
"Oh dear, I'd hoped the rumors about your illness weren't true," the king said.

47
00:03:52.215 --> 00:03:57.248
"But this is worse than I'd expected. Come here."

48
00:03:57.249 --> 00:04:01.985
Trembling, Tom went and stood in front of King Henry.

49
00:04:01.986 --> 00:04:08.500
"Prince Edward, tell me that you recognize your father," the king said.

50
00:04:08.501 --> 00:04:12.065
Tom took a deep breath.

51
00:04:12.066 --> 00:04:17.425
"I hope that you'll believe me, Your Majesty, but I'm not Prince Edward.

52
00:04:17.426 --> 00:04:21.512
I'm only one of your subjects from the poorest part of the city.

53
00:04:21.513 --> 00:04:24.454
Please don't send me to prison.

54
00:04:24.455 --> 00:04:30.013
I'm too young to spend the rest of my life there."

55
00:04:30.014 --> 00:04:36.650
"Send my son to prison? Don't be ridiculous," the king said.

56
00:04:36.651 --> 00:04:43.028
Tom was relieved but still uncertain. "Then I'm free to go?"

57
00:04:43.029 --> 00:04:46.785
"Go where?" King Henry asked.

58
00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:50.218
"Home, Your Majesty."

59
00:04:50.219 --> 00:04:53.862
Baffled, the king turned to Lord Hertford.

60
00:04:53.863 --> 00:04:57.702
"What do you think is the matter?"

61
00:04:57.703 --> 00:05:02.955
"Perhaps only part of the prince's mind is confused.

62
00:05:02.956 --> 00:05:10.890
Your Majesty could ask him about something other than yourself," Lord Hertford suggested.

63
00:05:10.891 --> 00:05:16.669
King Henry nodded and asked Tom a question in Latin.

64
00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:20.575
With some hesitation, Tom responded correctly.

65
00:05:20.576 --> 00:05:23.672
"Excellent!" the king said.

66
00:05:23.673 --> 00:05:32.537
"Now try this." He asked another question in French.

67
00:05:32.538 --> 00:05:40.447
"I'm sorry," Tom said, "but I don't even know what language you're speaking."

68
00:05:40.448 --> 00:05:48.276
King Henry frowned. "Too much studying has obviously caused this problem, Lord Hertford!

69
00:05:48.277 --> 00:05:53.270
No more lessons for Prince Edward until his health returns.

70
00:05:53.271 --> 00:06:00.180
In the meantime," he said to Tom, "what have you done with the Great Seal?"

71
00:06:00.181 --> 00:06:05.256
"The Great Seal?" Tom asked, confused.

72
00:06:05.257 --> 00:06:09.139
"Yes, you wanted to look at it last week.

73
00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:14.809
But I need it so I can place my seal on the death warrant of the Duke of Norfolk.

74
00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:19.827
I would like my enemy to die before I do."

75
00:06:19.828 --> 00:06:28.471
Tom bit his lip. "I have no idea where it is—or what it is."

76
00:06:28.472 --> 00:06:35.032
"Perhaps Your Majesty could use the Small Seal," Lord Hertford suggested.

77
00:06:35.033 --> 00:06:38.684
"Yes, yes, I know that."

78
00:06:38.685 --> 00:06:46.854
King Henry seemed tired and impatient. "Please leave."

79
00:06:46.855 --> 00:06:52.984
Lord Hertford signaled for Tom to bow to the king.

80
00:06:52.985 --> 00:06:57.610
"I'm a prisoner in this palace," Tom thought.

81
00:06:57.611 --> 00:07:06.899
"And I'll never be set free!"

